Package: steCI
Title: Confidence Intervals for Sequential Trial Emulation with Additive Hazards
Version: 0.0.1
Authors@R: c(
    person("M. Ehsan", "Karim", email = "ehsan7x7@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre")))
Description: Estimation of marginal risk differences and constant hazard
    differences via sequential trial emulation (STE) using weighted Aalen
    additive hazards models, for time-to-event outcomes with a monotone
    time-varying treatment and a time-varying confounder. Provides several
    confidence-interval procedures for the causal estimands: model-based,
    robust and cluster-robust analytic standard errors, the nonparametric
    (subject-level) bootstrap, the jackknife, and a linearised
    estimating-function / multiplier (wild) bootstrap with pointwise intervals
    and simultaneous confidence bands for the marginal risk-difference curve.
    Includes
    helpers to simulate data from an additive-hazard marginal structural
    model (Keogh et al. 2021), to expand longitudinal data into sequentially
    emulated trials, and to compute stabilized inverse-probability-of-
    artificial-censoring weights. Reimplements, with citation, the estimator
    of Keogh et al. (2023) <doi:10.1002/sim.9718> and the confidence-interval
    comparison framework of Limozin, Seaman and Su (2025)
    <doi:10.1177/09622802251356594>.
